1
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:37,500
To find her son, she did what no one else dared.

2
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:09,000
Changeling is a crime, drama, mystery film directed by Clint Eastwood.

3
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:40,500
Los Angeles, 1928.

4
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:12,000
When single mother Christine Collins leaves for
work, her son vanishes without a trace.

5
00:17:37,500 --> 00:17:43,500
Five months later, the police reunite mother and son.

6
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:15,000
But when Christine suspects that the boy returned to her isn't her
child, her quest for truth exposes a world of corruption.

7
00:24:40,500 --> 00:24:46,500
Christine Collins, played by Angelina Jolie.

8
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:18,000
Rev. Gustav Briegleb, played by John Malkovich.

9
00:31:43,500 --> 00:31:49,500
Captain J.J. Jones, played by Jeffrey Donovan.

10
00:35:15,000 --> 00:35:21,000
Detective Lester Ybarra, played by Michael Kelly.

11
00:38:46,500 --> 00:38:52,500
Chief James E. Davis, played by Colm Feore.

12
00:42:18,000 --> 00:42:24,000
Gordon Northcott, played by Jason Butler Harner.

13
00:45:49,500 --> 00:45:55,500
Changeling is a 2008 American mystery and crime drama film directed,
produced, and scored by Clint Eastwood and written by J.

14
00:49:21,000 --> 00:49:27,000
Michael Straczynski.

15
00:52:52,500 --> 00:52:58,500
The story was based on real-life events, specifically the 1928
Wineville Chicken Coop murders in Mira Loma, California.

16
00:56:24,000 --> 00:56:30,000
It stars Angelina Jolie as a woman united with a boy
who she realizes is not her missing son.

17
00:59:55,500 --> 01:00:01,500
When she tries to demonstrate that to the police and city authorities, she is vilified as
delusional, labeled as an unfit mother and confined to a psychiatric ward.

18
01:03:27,000 --> 01:03:33,000
The film explores themes of child endangerment, female disempowerment,
political corruption, and mistreatment of mental health patients.

19
01:06:58,500 --> 01:07:04,500
Working in 1983 as a special correspondent for the now defunct TV-Cable Week magazine, Straczynski first
learned the story of Christine Collins and her son from a Los Angeles City Hall contact.

20
01:10:30,000 --> 01:10:36,000
Over the ensuing years he kept researching the story but
never felt he was ready to tackle it.

21
01:14:01,500 --> 01:14:07,500
Out of television writing for several years and known to be difficult to work with, he
returned to researching and then finally writing the story in 2006.

22
01:17:33,000 --> 01:17:39,000
Almost all of the film's script was drawn from
thousands of pages of documentation.

23
01:21:04,500 --> 01:21:10,500
Ron Howard had intended to direct the film, but scheduling
conflicts led to his replacement by Eastwood.

24
01:24:36,000 --> 01:24:42,000
Howard and his Imagine Entertainment partner Brian Grazer produced Changeling
alongside Malpaso Productions' Robert Lorenz and Eastwood.

25
01:28:07,500 --> 01:28:13,500
Universal Pictures financed and distributed the film.

26
01:31:39,000 --> 01:31:45,000
Several actors campaigned for the leading role; ultimately, Eastwood
decided that Jolie's face would suit the 1920s period setting.

27
01:35:10,500 --> 01:35:16,500
The film also stars Jeffrey Donovan, Jason Butler Harner,
John Malkovich, Michael Kelly and Amy Ryan.

28
01:38:42,000 --> 01:38:48,000
While some characters are composites, most are based on actual people.

29
01:42:13,500 --> 01:42:19,500
Principal photography, which began on October 15, 2007, and concluded a few weeks later in
December, took place in Los Angeles and other locations in southern California.

30
01:45:45,000 --> 01:45:51,000
Actors and crew noted that Eastwood's low-key direction
resulted in a calm set and short working days.

31
01:49:16,500 --> 01:49:22,500
In post production, scenes were supplemented with
computer-generated skylines, backgrounds, vehicles and people.

32
01:52:48,000 --> 01:52:54,000
Changeling premiered to critical acclaim at the 61st
Cannes Film Festival on May 20, 2008.

33
01:56:19,500 --> 01:56:25,500
Additional festival screenings preceded a limited release in the United States on October 24, 2008, followed by a general release in
North America on October 31, 2008; in the United Kingdom on November 26, 2008; and in Australia on February 5, 2009.

34
01:59:51,000 --> 01:59:57,000
Critical reaction was more mixed than at Cannes.

35
02:03:22,500 --> 02:03:28,500
While the acting and story were generally praised, the film's
"conventional staging" and "lack of nuance" were criticized.

36
02:06:54,000 --> 02:07:00,000
Changeling earned $113 million in box-office revenue worldwide—of which
$35.7 million came from the United States and Canada.

37
02:10:25,500 --> 02:10:31,500
Changeling earned Jolie numerous award nominations including the Academy Award for Best Actress, the BAFTA Award for Best Actress in a Leading Role, the Critics' Choice Movie Award for Best
Actress, the Golden Globe Award for Best Actress in a Motion Picture – Drama and the Screen Actors Guild Award for Outstanding Performance by a Female Actor in a Leading Role.

38
02:13:57,000 --> 02:14:03,000
The film explores themes of biography, based on true story,
clergyman, child in peril, police corruption.

39
02:17:28,500 --> 02:17:34,500
The tone is emotional and mind_bending.
